Using dependency injection with abstractions

- So while using Spring Framework every object need not to be in the context
- Yes adding object to the context will give access to the Spring to use them but Spring doesnt need all objects to use
- So the question that should be raised is

“Does this object need to be managed by the framework?”

In this project we just used DI feature of Spring to do our work. So adding most of the object into context wont make anything bad

Only "Comment" object doesnt need the DI and its not a Dependency

The other objects in our class design are as
follows:
- CommentService—Has two dependencies, the CommentRepository and the CommentNotificationProxy
- DBCommentRepository—Implements the CommentRepository interface and is a dependency of the CommentService
- EmailCommentNotificationProxy—Implements the CommentNotificationProxy interface and is a dependency of the
CommentService


And another important not is not everything needed to be noted as Stereotype or Annotated eg @Component
Stereotype is only needed when The Spring Context need it to be Instantiated since the interface class wont be instantiated
they dont need to be marked as Stereotype or Annotated